      {
        "variation": "default",
        "version": "initial",
        "items": [],
        "primary": {
          "eyebrow": "Keep it chromatic and keep it simple",
          "title": "No notes left out",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Most hand-turned organs copy an old scale. To keep the price and the case small, they leave notes out. The scale is then no longer chromatic, and that has two consequences:",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "list-item",
              "text": "You cannot transpose a song to another key.",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "list-item",
              "text": "Many songs lose notes, so the arranger has to make compromises you can hear.",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Our Bellow Organ keeps every note. Any arrangement written for its range plays as written, in the key you choose.",
              "spans": []
            }
          ],
          "image": {
            "dimensions": {
              "width": 1237,
              "height": 709
